    {
      "title": "China's intelligence arm ran campaign to acquire advanced AI chips: Report",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/china-s-intelligence-arm-ran-campaign-to-acquire-advanced-ai-chips-report-126112200365_1.html",
      "description": "China's intelligence agency has made acquiring advanced semiconductor chips and gathering intelligence on the global chip industry a priority, running a campaign to overcome Western export restrictions for at least two years, according to a New York Times (NYT) report.\nThe Ministry of State Security (MSS) set up a working group under its chief Chen Yixin to lead the effort, which includes helping Chinese companies acquire and smuggle advanced chips into the country, besides collecting intelligence on the semiconductor sector and its supply chains, the report said, citing serving and former security and intelligence officials from Asia, the US and Europe.\nThe revelations come amid US scrutiny of Chinese businesswoman Alice Huang, whom American officials allege was working with the Chinese intelligence agency to spy on Jensen Huang, Nvidia's co-founder and former chief executive.\nThe NYT report, published on Saturday, adds to findings published by the newspaper on November 20, which .",
